d\": 62685, \"t_start\": 57886, \"value\": 12}, {\"t_end\": 67485, \"t_start\": 62686, \"value\": 8}, {\"t_end\": 72285, \"t_start\": 67486, \"value\": 7}, {\"t_end\": 77085, \"t_start\": 72286, \"value\": 8}, {\"t_end\": 81885, \"t_start\": 77086, \"value\": 20}, {\"t_end\": 86685, \"t_start\": 81886, \"value\": 33}], \"metric\": \"event_count\", \"window\": [48286, 86685]}", "latency_ms": 1, "tokens_before": 44721, "tokens_after": 44721, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_9a10daa0", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [1800, 1115], "window": [48286, 86685], "confidence": 0.92, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade from 1800 to 1115 within [48286,86685] under the 600-unit gap limit. Reachability at delta=600 yields 82 reached nodes excluding 1115, and path enumeration returns nothing. The failure is robust: delta=1500 and delta=3000 also fail. Unconstrained, a route does exist (1800->801->1071->1706->1115) but its hop waits are 4788/4699/3010, each ~5-8x over budget; enumerated alternatives end with a 359->1115 hop idling ~15,700 units. Confounders are controlled: both endpoints are highly active (71 and 69 events, 70 out- and 67 in-neighbors) in a dense 7,760-event window, so this is not data sparsity; and although a static 2-hop bridge via node 36 appears, the second leg is directed 1115->36 rather than 36->1115, so even the ignore-time connection is not a valid influence channel. Static adjacency and node popularity are present, but the temporal structure required for influence transmission is not."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**No genuine cascade exists.** The evidence is consistent and decisive:\n\n1. **Direct test fails (step_01, step_13):** Under the \u0394\u2264600 constraint, 1800 reaches only 82 nodes \u2014 and 1115 is not among them.\n2. **No paths enumerated (step_05):** Path enumeration at \u0394=600 returns an empty set, confirming the negative rather than a search artifact.\n3. **Relaxation sweep (step_07, step_08):** Even at \u0394=1500 and \u0394=3000 \u2014 2.5\u00d7 and 5\u00d7 the allowed gap \u2014 1115 remains unreachable. The failure is robust, not marginal.\n4. **The connection is real but far too slow (step_03):** Unconstrained, a route exists (1800\u2192801\u21921071\u21921706\u21921115) with hop waits of **4788, 4699, 3010** \u2014 every single hop violates the 600-unit budget by roughly an order of magnitude. Enumerated alternatives (step_12) are worse, with a final dangling hop 359\u21921115 that idles ~15,700 units.\n\n**Confounders ruled out:**\n- *Not sparse data:* both endpoints are highly active \u2014 71 and 69 events, 70 out-neighbors and 67 in-neighbors respectively (step_04, step_06, step_09), within a dense 7,760-event window (step_02). Failure isn't from missing activity.\n- *Not static disconnection:* the two are statically linked at short range (step_10), including an apparent 2-hop bridge via 36. But that bridge collapses on inspection: 1800\u219236 exists (step_14) while the second leg runs **1115\u219236**, not 36\u21921115 (step_15) \u2014 wrong direction entirely. Static adjacency is a mirage here.\n- *Not a timing-window mismatch:* both nodes are active early and late (step_16), so their activity does overlap in time; the gaps are genuinely in the connecting chain.\n\nThe static connection and high node popularity are exactly the misleading signals the task warns about \u2014 neither survives the temporal constraint.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9a10daa0\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1800, 1115],\n  \"window\": [48286, 86685],\n  \"confidence\": 0.92,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade from 1800 to 1115 within [48286,86685] under the 600-unit gap limit. Reachability at delta=600 yields 82 reached nodes excluding 1115, and path enumeration returns nothing. The failure is robust: delta=1500 and delta=3000 also fail. Unconstrained, a route does exist (1800->801->1071->1706->1115) but its hop waits are 4788/4699/3010, each ~5-8x over budget; enumerated alternatives end with a 359->1115 hop idling ~15,700 units. Confounders are controlled: both endpoints are highly active (71 and 69 events, 70 out- and 67 in-neighbors) in a dense 7,760-event window, so this is not data sparsity; and although a static 2-hop bridge via node 36 appears, the second leg is directed 1115->36 rather than 36->1115, so even the ignore-time connection is not a valid influence channel. Static adjacency and node popularity are present, but the temporal structure required for influence transmission is not.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 55469, "total_output_tokens": 4311, "total_tokens": 59780, "total_latency_ms": 61276, "llm_calls": 8, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}